│ Okay, let’s address this. Based on the       │
│ previous conversation and the understanding  │
│ that Django 2.2+ changed the behavior of     │
│ get_FIELD_display(), the issue is that it’s  │
│ no longer called when using __str__. The fix │
│ is to explicitly call get_FIELD_display()    │
│ within the __str__ method.                   │
│                                              │
│ Here’s the reasoning:                        │
│                                              │
│ The core problem is that Django 2.2+ doesn't │
│ automatically call get_FIELD_display() when  │
│ using __str__.  The original code relied on  │
│ this implicit behavior, which is now broken. │
│ To fix this, we need to explicitly call      │
│ get_FIELD_display() within the __str__       │
│ method to ensure that the correct display    │
│ value is returned.                           │
